  "A policy records who is covered, for what risk, the sum insured, the start and end dates and the premium. Changes during the term are endorsements, and renewals create a new policy term, so a policy has many versions. Written premium is booked when a policy is sold; earned premium is the part that matches time already covered, so a 12-month policy sold today is only one-twelfth earned after a month. Claims have a loss date, a report date, payments and reserves, which are the insurer's estimate of what is still to be paid. IBNR (incurred but not reported) reserves cover losses that have happened but not yet been claimed. In India, insurers are regulated by IRDAI, and sales flow through agents, brokers, banks and online channels.",
